From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Adrian <4.adam.adrian@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Sep 2026 23:15:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov8865: Invert horizontal flip polarity on
 Microsoft Surface devices

On Microsoft Surface devices (Surface Pro 4/5/6, Surface Go 2/3), the
OV8865 rear camera sensor is mounted such that libcamera's automatic
HFlip (triggered by camera_sensor_rotation=180) results in a horizontally
mirrored image.

Invert the horizontal flip control polarity when running on Microsoft
Surface hardware so that the physical sensor register receives a no-flip
value (0) when libcamera requests HFlip=1, producing a natural, upright,
non-mirrored image.

Patchset: cameras-local
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov8865.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov8865.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/device.h>
+#include <linux/dmi.h>
 #include <linux/i2c.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of_graph.h>
@@ -2202,11 +2203,24 @@
 				  enable ? bits : 0);
 }
 
+static const struct dmi_system_id ov8865_surface_dmi[] = {
+	{
+		.ident = "Microsoft Surface Devices",
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "Microsoft Corporation"),
+		},
+	},
+	{}
+};
+
 static int ov8865_flip_horz_configure(struct ov8865_sensor *sensor, bool enable)
 {
 	u8 bits = OV8865_FORMAT2_FLIP_HORZ_ISP_EN |
 		  OV8865_FORMAT2_FLIP_HORZ_SENSOR_EN;
 
+	if (dmi_check_system(ov8865_surface_dmi))
+		enable = !enable;
+
 	return ov8865_update_bits(sensor, OV8865_FORMAT2_REG, bits,
 				  enable ? bits : 0);
 }
